-> Test: unary minus / negative number literals.
x = -5
assert x ≠ 1
assert x ≠ 5

-> Precedence: unary minus binds tighter than `*`.
assert -5 * 2 = -10

-> Existing binary subtraction is unchanged.
a = 10
b = 3
c = a - b
assert c = 7

-> Mixed: subtracting a negative literal.
r = a - -5
assert r = 15

-> Double negation.
assert - -5 = 5

-> Negative literals inside an array.
arr = [-1, -2, -3]
assert arr[0] = -1
assert arr[2] = -3
